          %h3#existence_and_uniqueness Existence and Uniqueness
          %p
            Any locally compact Hausdorff topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            admits a Haar integral (and therefore Haar measure) that is unique up to scalar multiple. This result was first proven by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"} André Weil
            %a{:href => "#Alfsen63"} Alfsen 1963
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"}> consructive
            ) and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Rubinstein-Salzedo04"} Rubinstein-Salzedo 2004
          %p
